      "role": "user",
      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS\n- LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- TIP_DETAIL\n\n## Column Mapping\n- enrollment type: IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL.ENROLLMENT_TYPE\n- Advance sign-up required: IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL.ENROLLMENT_TYPE\n- maximum enrollment: IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL.MAX_ENROLLMENT\n- 12: IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL.MAX_ENROLLMENT\n- activity title: IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL.ACTIVITY_TITLE\n- term code: IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL.TERM_CODE\n- term description: ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_DESCRIPTION\n- term start date: ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_START_DATE\n- subject title: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_TITLE\n- number of enrolled students: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- offer department name: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\n- responsible faculty name: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_NAME\n- window column: IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL.ACTIVITY_TITLE, LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_TITLE\n- highest number of associated course materials: TIP_DETAIL.TIP_MATERIAL_KEY\n- number of enrolled students is at least 10: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- order the results by activity title within each subject title group: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_TITLE, IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL.ACTIVITY_TITLE\n\n## Join Keys\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE <-> IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL.TERM_CODE\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE <-> LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE <-> TIP_DETAIL.TERM_CODE\n\n## Subquery Decomposition\n1. For subjects with an enrollment type of \"Advance sign-up required\" and a maximum enrollment of 12, show the subject's activity title, term code, maximum enrollment, term description, term start date, subject title, number of enrolled students, and assign row numbers within each subject title group ordered by activity title.\n```sql\nSELECT t0.ACTIVITY_TITLE, t0.TERM_CODE, t0.MAX_ENROLLMENT, t1.TERM_DESCRIPTION, t1.TERM_START_DATE, t2.SUBJECT_TITLE, t2.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS, ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY t2.SUBJECT_TITLE ORDER BY t0.ACTIVITY_TITLE) AS window_column FROM IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL t0 JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS t1 ON t0.TERM_CODE = t1.TERM_CODE JOIN LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED t2 ON t1.TERM_CODE = t2.TERM_CODE WHERE t0.ENROLLMENT_TYPE = 'Advance sign-up required' AND t0.MAX_ENROLLMENT = 12\n```\n2. Which are the top 10 activity titles with the highest number of associated course materials, including the activity title from IAP subject details, the term description from academic terms, and the count of course materials from TIP detail?\n```sql\nSELECT IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL.ACTIVITY_TITLE, ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_DESCRIPTION, COUNT(TIP_DETAIL.TIP_MATERIAL_KEY) AS material_count FROM IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS ON IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL.TERM_CODE = ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE JOIN TIP_DETAIL ON ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE = TIP_DETAIL.TERM_CODE WHERE IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL.IS_CANCELLED = 'N' GROUP BY IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL.ACTIVITY_TITLE, ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_DESCRIPTION ORDER BY material_count DESC LIMIT 10;\n```\n3. For subjects with an enrollment type of \"Advance sign-up required\" and a maximum enrollment of 12, show the subject's activity title, term code, maximum enrollment, term description, term start date, subject title, number of enrolled students, and, for each, also include the offer department name and responsible faculty name. Only include results where the number of enrolled students is at least 10, and order the results by activity title within each subject title group.\n```sql\nWITH inner_cte AS ( SELECT t0.ACTIVITY_TITLE, t0.TERM_CODE, t0.MAX_ENROLLMENT, t1.TERM_DESCRIPTION, t1.TERM_START_DATE, t2.SUBJECT_TITLE, t2.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS, ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY t2.SUBJECT_TITLE ORDER BY t0.ACTIVITY_TITLE) AS window_column FROM IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL t0 JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS t1 ON t0.TERM_CODE = t1.TERM_CODE JOIN LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED t2 ON t1.TERM_CODE = t2.TERM_CODE WHERE t0.ENROLLMENT_TYPE = 'Advance sign-up required' AND t0.MAX_ENROLLMENT = 12 ) SELECT inner_cte.ACTIVITY_TITLE, inner_cte.TERM_CODE, inner_cte.MAX_ENROLLMENT, inner_cte.TERM_DESCRIPTION, inner_cte.TERM_START_DATE, inner_cte.SUBJECT_TITLE, inner_cte.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS, t2.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, t2.RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_NAME, inner_cte.window_column FROM inner_cte JOIN LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED t2 ON inner_cte.TERM_CODE = t2.TERM_CODE AND inner_cte.SUBJECT_TITLE = t2.SUBJECT_TITLE WHERE inner_cte.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS >= 10 ORDER BY inner_cte.SUBJECT_TITLE, inner_cte.ACTIVITY_TITLE;\n```\n4. For each activity title, what is the highest number of associated course materials it has had in any term, including the activity title from IAP subject details and the maximum material count?\n```sql\nWITH inner_cte AS ( SELECT IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL.ACTIVITY_TITLE, ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_DESCRIPTION, COUNT(TIP_DETAIL.TIP_MATERIAL_KEY) AS material_count FROM IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS ON IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL.TERM_CODE = ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE JOIN TIP_DETAIL ON ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE = TIP_DETAIL.TERM_CODE WHERE IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL.IS_CANCELLED = 'N' GROUP BY IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL.ACTIVITY_TITLE, ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_DESCRIPTION ) SELECT ACTIVITY_TITLE, MAX(material_count) AS highest_material_count FROM inner_cte GROUP BY ACTIVITY_TITLE;\n```\n\n## Question\nFor subjects with an enrollment type of \"Advance sign-up required\" and a maximum enrollment of 12, show the subject's activity title, term code, maximum enrollment, term description, term start date, subject title, number of enrolled students, offer department name, responsible faculty name, window column, and, for each activity title, also include the highest number of associated course materials it has had in any term. Only include results where the number of enrolled students is at least 10, and order the results by activity title within each subject title group. Do not return any rounded answers."
