  "content": "# Final Report\n\n## 1. Entity Semantics\n\n**Tables (Phase 1 survivors):**\n\n| ID | Semantics | Key columns |\n|---|---|---|\n| `IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL` | One row per IAP activity offered in a January term | ACTIVITY_TITLE, TERM_CODE, ENROLLMENT_TYPE (e.g. 'Advance sign-up required'), MAX_ENROLLMENT, IS_CANCELLED |\n| `ACADEMIC_TERMS` | Academic term dimension with calendar/status attributes | TERM_CODE, TERM_DESCRIPTION, TERM_START_DATE, TERM_END_DATE, TERM_STATUS |\n| `LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED` | Subjects per term in library reserve processing scope | SUBJECT_ID, SUBJECT_TITLE, TERM_CODE, OFFER_DEPT_NAME, RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_NAME, NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS |\n| `TIP_DETAIL` | Subject-material-status rows of the textbook program | TIP_MATERIAL_KEY, TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY, TERM_CODE, SUBJECT_ID, RECORD_COUNT |\n| `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED` | TIP program subject-level parent of TIP_DETAIL | SUBJECT_ID, TERM_CODE, NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS, IS_NO_COURSE_MATERIAL |\n\n**Concepts:** `concept_iap_activities`, `concept_subject_offering_facts`, `concept_course_material_programs`, `concept_academic_term_dimension` — retrieved in full; decision guides confirm: IAP enrollment-type/capacity questions → IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL; term description/start date → ACADEMIC_TERMS; library-scope enrollment → LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS; material counts → COUNT(TIP_DETAIL.TIP_MATERIAL_KEY).\n\n**Column concepts:** `column_concept_enrollment_measures` (NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS = program-scope headcount; LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED's is the library snapshot — exactly what the question's \"number of enrolled students\" maps to per the hint), `column_concept_term_code` (TERM_CODE is the universal join key across IAP/terms/library/TIP), `column_concept_subject_id`, `column_concept_department_name` (OFFER_DEPT_NAME is the library/TIP academic-department naming convention), `column_concept_material_status_key`.\n\n**Metrics investigated:** `dw_4069`, `dw_3736`, `dw_3959`, `dw_3436` (full SQL retrieved); `dw_2790`, `dw_3612`, `dw_4558` (descriptions retrieved).\n\n## 2. Lineage & Relationships\n\n- `semantic_graph(IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL, both)`: joins → ACADEMIC_TERMS, ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL, LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED, TIP_DETAIL, TIME_DAY, IAP child tables; concept ← concept_iap_activities; column_concept ← column_concept_term_code. This confirms the exact join path in the hints (IAP↔terms↔library↔TIP all via TERM_CODE).\n- `semantic_graph(LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED, both)`: joins → ACADEMIC_TERMS, TIP_DETAIL, TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SIS_DEPARTMENT; incoming from IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL, LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL; concepts ← concept_subject_offering_facts, concept_course_material_programs.\n- `semantic_graph(metrics_by_table, TIP_DETAIL)`: 41 dependent metrics, including dw_4069, dw_3736, dw_3436, dw_3612, dw_4558 — TIP_DETAIL is the established source for course-material counting (COUNT(TIP_MATERIAL_KEY) per the concept comparison \"Count measures\").\n\n## 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n\n**3a. Dimension matrix (enrollment measure candidates):**\n\n| Dimension | LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS | TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS | SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Meaning | Library-reserve-scope headcount snapshot | Textbook-program-scope snapshot | Official registrar enrollment |\n| Grain | per subject per term (library scope) | per subject per term (TIP scope) | per subject per term |\n| Companion fields | SUBJECT_TITLE, OFFER_DEPT_NAME, RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_NAME (all requested by task) | Same companions, but different program scope | No OFFER_DEPT_NAME/RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_NAME pairing requested here |\n| Evidence | column_concept_enrollment_measures decision_guide: \"library reserve scope → LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\" | same decision_guide | same decision_guide (\"official subject enrollment\") |\n\n**Term table candidates:** ACADEMIC_TERMS vs ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL — concept_academic_term_dimension comparison: ACADEMIC_TERMS carries TERM_STATUS/IS_REGULAR_TERM; both carry TERM_DESCRIPTION/TERM_START_DATE. All hint precedents (dw_4069, dw_3736, dw_3959) use ACADEMIC_TERMS for this exact task shape.\n\n**3b. Task-Requirement Fitness Mapping:**\n\n| Requirement | LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED | TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED | SUBJECT_SUMMARY |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| \"number of enrolled students\" ≥ 10 | SUPPORTED (NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) | SUPPORTED but wrong scope | SUPPORTED but different semantics (registrar) |\n| subject title / offer dept name / responsible faculty name | SUPPORTED (all three columns exist) | SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED (no OFFER_DEPT_NAME) |\n| join to IAP via TERM_CODE precedent | SUPPORTED (dw_4069/3736/3959 use it) | no precedent for this shape | no precedent |\n\n| Requirement | COUNT(TIP_DETAIL.TIP_MATERIAL_KEY) per activity+term, MAX over terms |\n|---|---|\n| \"highest number of associated course materials in any term\" | SUPPORTED — two-level aggregation per hint decomposition #2/#4; IS_CANCELLED='N' filter per precedent |\n\n**3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring:** \"number of enrolled students\" lexically matches NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS (column_concept_enrollment_measures); the requested companions (subject title, offer department name, responsible faculty name) all exist only together in LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED/TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED, and the hint column mapping explicitly anchors them to LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED. \"window column\" anchors to ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY SUBJECT_TITLE ORDER BY ACTIVITY_TITLE) per dw_4069/dw_3736/dw_3959 precedent. \"highest number of associated course materials ... in any term\" anchors to MAX over per-(ACTIVITY_TITLE, TERM_DESCRIPTION) COUNT(TIP_MATERIAL_KEY).\n\n**3d. Precedent Usage Evidence:** The identical inner CTE (IAP 'Advance sign-up required' + MAX_ENROLLMENT=12 joined to ACADEMIC_TERMS and LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED on TERM_CODE with ROW_NUMBER window) appears verbatim in 3 metrics: dw_4069, dw_3736, dw_3959. dw_3959 additionally uses the exact NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS ≥ 10 filter, the OFFER_DEPT_NAME/RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_NAME re-join on TERM_CODE+SUBJECT_TITLE, and ORDER BY SUBJECT_TITLE, ACTIVITY_TITLE. Material-count-per-activity precedent: hint decompositions #2/#4 (COUNT(TIP_MATERIAL_KEY), IS_CANCELLED='N', GROUP BY ACTIVITY_TITLE+TERM_DESCRIPTION, then MAX per ACTIVITY_TITLE).\n\n## 4. Business Usage\n\n- **IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL**: consumed by IAP capacity/enrollment-type metrics (dw_2790, dw_3047, dw_2858, dw_4069, dw_3736, dw_3959...); serves \"which activities match filter X\" patterns.\n- **ACADEMIC_TERMS**: universal term enrichment (description, start date) in nearly all subject/activity metrics.\n- **LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED**: library-scope enrollment and faculty attribution; parent of reserve detail; used in dw_4069/dw_3736/dw_3959/dw_3393 etc.\n- **TIP_DETAIL**: 41 dependent metrics; the standard course-material counting table (COUNT(TIP_MATERIAL_KEY) per concept decision guide).\n- **TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED**: TIP-scope subject attributes; not needed here since material counting uses TIP_DETAIL directly per precedent.\n\n## 5. Coverage Checklist\n\n| Entity | Tools called |\n|---|---|\n| IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL | semantic_search, semantic_get, semantic_graph (neighbors) |\n| ACADEMIC_TERMS | semantic_search, semantic_get, semantic_graph (via neighbors) |\n| LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED | semantic_search, semantic_get, semantic_graph (neighbors) |\n| TIP_DETAIL | semantic_search, semantic_get, semantic_graph (metrics_by_table: 41 metrics) |\n| TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED | semantic_search, semantic_get |\n| concept_iap_activities / concept_course_material_programs / concept_academic_term_dimension / concept_subject_offering_facts | semantic_get / graph neighbors |\n| column_concept_enrollment_measures / term_code / subject_id / department_name / material_status_key | semantic_get / graph neighbors |\n| dw_4069, dw_3736, dw_3959, dw_3436 | semantic_get (full SQL) |\n| dw_2790, dw_3612, dw_4558, dw_2858, dw_3047 etc. | semantic_search descriptions |\n\nNote: `mysql_query` verification was attempted repeatedly but the database returned \"Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost'\" on every call (including `SELECT 1` and `SHOW TABLES`), so live data verification was impossible; the SQL follows the verified gold-precedent structure exactly.\n\n## 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a. Tables/columns:** IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL (ACTIVITY_TITLE, TERM_CODE, MAX_ENROLLMENT, ENROLLMENT_TYPE filter, IS_CANCELLED filter for the material CTE), ACADEMIC_TERMS (TERM_DESCRIPTION, TERM_START_DATE), LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED (SUBJECT_TITLE, NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS, OFFER_DEPT_NAME, RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_NAME), TIP_DETAIL (TIP_MATERIAL_KEY count).\n\n**6b. SQL approach:** Three CTEs mirroring the hint decomposition: (1) `inner_cte` — IAP filtered to 'Advance sign-up required'/MAX_ENROLLMENT=12, joined to ACADEMIC_TERMS and LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED on TERM_CODE, with ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY SUBJECT_TITLE ORDER BY ACTIVITY_TITLE); (2) `subq1` — re-join LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED on TERM_CODE+SUBJECT_TITLE to attach OFFER_DEPT_NAME/RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_NAME, filter NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS ≥ 10; (3) `subq2` — two-level aggregation: inner counts TIP_MATERIAL_KEY per (ACTIVITY_TITLE, TERM_DESCRIPTION) for non-cancelled activities joined to TIP_DETAIL via ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE, outer takes MAX per ACTIVITY_TITLE. Final: join subq1↔subq2 on ACTIVITY_TITLE, ORDER BY SUBJECT_TITLE, ACTIVITY_TITLE. SELECT list = exactly the 11 requested columns in asked order.\n\n**6c. Reasons:** *Data*: all required columns physically exist in these tables (verified via semantic_get column definitions); TERM_CODE joins are documented 1:many-safe per precedent. *Semantic-network*: graph edges confirm IAP↔ACADEMIC_TERMS↔LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED↔TIP_DETAIL joins; enrollment-measures decision guide anchors \"number of enrolled students\" to LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED. *Business*: dw_3959 is a near-identical precedent (same filters, same ≥10 threshold, same ordering), and dw_4069/dw_3736 reuse the same inner CTE verbatim.\n\n**6d. Alternatives:** TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED could supply enrollment/faculty but no precedent uses it for this shape and the hint mapping explicitly names LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED; ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL lacks nothing needed here but precedents use ACADEMIC_TERMS. No genuine tie.\n\nThe final SQL was submitted via `submit_SQL` (accepted as case dw_4413).",
